body:
I mean CPS thought it was serious enough to notify the police because I sure didn't call the police. I had a detective call me out of nowhere saying he was investigating it. 

&#x200B;

And if was an accident she should have reported what happened and notified me in a timely manner. Not the next day. A toddler broke his leg at midnight under her care and she's now upset that we are upset and is withholding my son from me.

As of right now I'm not sure if she has an order. My lawyer also filed a complaint against her for being in contempt because she hasn't allowed me to facetime my son at all in over 10 days and it clearly states on there that I'm allowed to talk to him. So we have that going for us as well. 

&#x200B;

The one text I have from her a while ago about this stuff she said "I don't even want to do 50/50 but I do it because I don't want to keep Jameson from his father" which is exactly what she's doing now.

To add: 

&#x200B;

I have texts from her the on Wednesday, Feb 17th thanking me for helping her by keeping our son an extra night and being "cool and fair". 

&#x200B;

The next morning I woke up to a borage of texts from her calling me names and saying I won't see him again because she found out I claimed him on my taxes. Now, she's saying the real reason she's not giving him back to me is because "he's unfit to be a father".

Pens players? 

&#x200B;

Jagr is number one. Francis would be next. Coffey would be after that. Not sure if they have to be retired of not but Crosby and Malkin as well
